{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Bird</b> — and afterward he mentions the fowl, that flies above him, and the fish that swims below him." "And the meaning of עֹבֵר אָרְחוֹת יַמִּים — that in his wisdom he makes ships and knows the paths of the seas, and he mentions this because he catches fish in the heart of the sea. And some say: that it speaks of the fish, that passes over the paths of the seas."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:40.207722873Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}